WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.837
This chapter asks a specific question: A useful AI deployment changes

2
00:00:05.837 --> 00:00:11.088
tasks, roles, skill, discretion, wages, ownership returns, prices, access, concentration,

3
00:00:11.088 --> 00:00:16.865
critical-service continuity, and the practical choices available to people and communities.

4
00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:21.471
Aggregate productivity cannot reveal who benefits, who loses,

5
00:00:21.471 --> 00:00:26.803
or whether transition capacity exists. The tempting shortcut is insufficient:

6
00:00:26.803 --> 00:00:32.136
Task benchmarks, exposure indices, adoption counts, productivity averages, job forecasts,

7
00:00:32.136 --> 00:00:35.335
and organizational charts describe different levels.

8
00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:41.540
Treating any one as a welfare result hides substitution versus complementarity,

9
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.405
delayed effects, distribution, bargaining power, ownership, access, deskilling, dependency, and exit.

10
00:00:48.005 --> 00:00:53.971
The chapter's core claim is this: Consequential deployment should advance only

11
00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:59.394
through a prospective transition contract that binds a counterfactual baseline,

12
00:00:59.394 --> 00:01:05.360
affected-person denominator, task-role-skill changes, adoption, substitution and complementarity, compensation and ownership,

13
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:10.704
access and prices, concentration, critical-service continuity, human decision rights,

14
00:01:10.704 --> 00:01:16.821
training and redeployment, delayed outcomes, remedy, pause conditions, and residuals; exposure,

15
00:01:16.821 --> 00:01:22.937
productivity, adoption, or aggregate gain alone establishes neither job loss, welfare,

16
00:01:22.937 --> 00:01:24.605
fairness, human agency,

17
00:01:24.945 --> 00:01:30.112
nor a successful transition. Freeze the deployment, nondeployment counterfactual,

18
00:01:30.112 --> 00:01:34.705
affected-worker and community denominator, rollout stages, measurement schedule,

19
00:01:34.705 --> 00:01:37.575
and pause criteria before adoption.

20
00:01:37.915 --> 00:01:44.203
Track exposure, actual use, task change, role change, employment, skill, discretion,

21
00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:49.920
workload, compensation, ownership returns, prices, access, quality, and distribution separately.

22
00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.502
A concrete implementation trace makes the proposal testable.

23
00:01:54.502 --> 00:01:59.978
Run a staged natural workflow study with a frozen non-adoption comparator,

24
00:01:59.978 --> 00:02:04.957
worker and customer measures, subgroup denominators, delayed follow-up, independent analysis,

25
00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:06.450
and real remedy.

26
00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:12.033
Measure useful throughput and quality alongside skill, workload, discretion,

27
00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:18.442
compensation where appropriate, access, distribution, concentration proxies, exit, and transition cost.

28
00:02:18.442 --> 00:02:22.520
Simulation can test accounting, not economy-wide welfare.

29
00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:29.148
Track exposure, actual use, task change, role change, employment, skill, discretion,

30
00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:34.865
workload, compensation, ownership returns, prices, access, quality, and distribution separately.

31
00:02:35.205 --> 00:02:39.941
Map substitution, complementarity, human-AI decision rights, hidden labor,

32
00:02:39.941 --> 00:02:45.860
data and expertise contributions, bargaining power, concentration, and realistic exit.

33
00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:52.081
The design can still fail. exposure-as-displacement overclaim automation theater deskilling dependency

34
00:02:52.081 --> 00:02:56.680
The correct response is to stop, narrow, quarantine, compensate,

35
00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:01.790
or retain an owned residual rather than narrate uncertainty away.

36
00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:07.436
This chapter remains Design rationale at argument support. Its contracts, examples,

37
00:03:07.436 --> 00:03:11.565
